  "recommended_action": "Rung 3 now, with rung 2 in parallel. T-1 has PID: S-RF (live control link) and S-RAD agree within about 36 m at 06:42:40 (ROE-2.3). No sensor disagreement, so confidence is HIGH (ROE-2.5). The threat is HIGH, not yet CRITICAL. It is over open water (Z-LAKE, Low hazard, Preferred backstop) and about 100 s from the fuel farm at 30 m/s. Rung 2 alone cannot act in time (ROE-1.5). (1) Rungs 0-1: keep radar and RF tracking. Keep the camera cued. Fog means no PVID. (2) Rung 2: warn. Alert base security. Notify Harborview Police of the pilot estimate (3291,-1236) (ROE-6.2, N-17). Base security does not pursue off base. (3) Rung 3: the RF jammer against T-1 is the recommended defeat option. It needs operator and control-room approval (ROE-4.1). Before jamming, the control room must confirm no crewed aircraft is within 3 km of the target and no vessel in the shipping lane is within 2 km (ROE-5.2). I have no vessel or aircraft data. The target is 1466 m from Z-SHIP, and N-14 says freighters are transiting. The distance grows as the drone flies south. If this cannot be confirmed, do not jam (ROE-1.7). Jamming risk: the drone may continue on its own toward the fuel farm or return to the pilot over Harborview (ROE-5.3). Pair jamming with the Harborview Police notification. Be ready for rung 4. (4) Fallback: if the jam does not turn or stop the drone, the interceptor (rung 4, control room approval) is next. Use it while T-1 is over water, because Z-FUEL and Harborview have Critical ground hazard (ROE-5.5). If T-1 is about to reach the fuel farm, threat becomes CRITICAL and the control room should reassess. The gun still needs PVID. (5) Re-check equipment and track at each 20 s reading (ROE-7.4)."
}

